{% comment %}
  SS Anchor — section spacing.

  WHY THIS EXISTS: the theme's .index-section applies `margin: 60px 0`
  (assets/theme.css.liquid:7013, via --indexSectionPadding). Four of the copied
  sections carried that class and three carried their own padding, so the page
  rendered gaps of 60 / 146 / 60 / 60 instead of the design's even 48.

  This makes spacing come from exactly ONE place — the section's own
  padding_top / padding_bottom sliders — by:
    1. zeroing any .index-section margin inside the section, and
    2. applying the slider values as padding on the section wrapper.

  The id selector is (1,1,0), which beats .index-section at (0,1,0), so no
  !important is needed.

  Usage:
    {%- render 'ss-anchor-space', id: section.id,
        top: section.settings.padding_top, bottom: section.settings.padding_bottom -%}

  Params:
    - id     (required) section.id
    - top    (required) px
    - bottom (required) px
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign pt = top | default: 0
  assign pb = bottom | default: 0
-%}

{%- if id != blank -%}
  {%- style -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ id }} {
      margin-top: 0;
      margin-bottom: 0;
      padding-top: {{ pt }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ pb }}px;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ id }} .index-section,
    #shopify-section-{{ id }} .index-section + .index-section {
      margin-top: 0;
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
  {%- endstyle -%}
{%- endif -%}
